There lies a difference between the two.

If you want to play or finish the game for fun, then by all means,
save scum as much as you like. It's your game, and you might even meet
someone else who has the same mindset in playing the game as you are.

However, the community has all the right to tell you that what you are
doing is "cheating" or "wrong". If you want to gain respect and
validate your achievements in that community, you must abide by their
norms.

For example, the Starcraft community wouldn't mind restoring from
saves as there is a way to save to it. On the other hand, in the
NetHack community they would certainly consider it cheating if you
restore from a save after death, which is what your script does.

Even then, there's nothing inherently bad with the script; it's just
another way of playing the game. What earned its derision was your
justification that it's not wrong, when quite obviously the community
thinks it is.

